"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith=self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith||[]).push([[69459],{769459:n=>{n.exports='# Common Issues on Standard and Serverless Compute\n\nThese are confirmed bugs in the Spark Connect runtime or Databricks platform that affect\nStandard and Serverless compute. Unlike API surface incompatibilities, these are not\narchitectural limitations but implementation issues.\n\n## Pattern: display(df) with images\n\n**Severity:** P1\n**Affected Compute:** Standard, Serverless\n**Languages:** Both\n**DBR Fix Version:** None (tracked)\n\n### Incompatible Code\n\n```python\n# DataFrame containing image metadata columns\ndf = spark.read.format("image").load("/path/to/images")\ndisplay(df)\n```\n\n### Why It Fails\n\nRunning `display()` on a DataFrame with image metadata columns triggers an internal\nerror in the shared cluster display rendering pipeline. The Spark Connect command\nhandler does not properly support image-type columns in the display serialization path.\n\n### SC-Compatible Alternative\n\n```python\n# Drop image columns before display, or select only non-image columns\ndf = spark.read.format("image").load("/path/to/images")\ndisplay(df.drop("image"))\n\n# Or select specific columns\ndisplay(df.select("origin", "height", "width"))\n```\n\n### Notes\n\n- Error: `[UC_COMMAND_NOT_SUPPORTED.WITHOUT_RECOMMENDATION]`\n- This is a known platform bug, not a Spark Connect architectural limitation.\n\n---\n\n## Pattern: Pandas UDF row-wise yield in generator functions\n\n**Severity:** P1\n**Affected Compute:** Standard, Serverless\n**Languages:** Python\n**DBR Fix Version:** None (tracked)\n\n### Incompatible Code\n\n```python\nfrom pyspark.sql.functions import pandas_udf\nimport pandas as pd\nfrom typing import Iterator\n\n@pandas_udf("long")\ndef my_udf(iterator: Iterator[pd.Series]) -> Iterator[pd.Series]:\n    for batch in iterator:\n        # Row-wise yield instead of batch-wise yield\n        for val in batch:\n            yield pd.Series([val * 2])\n```\n\n### Why It Fails\n\nWhen a Pandas UDF generator function yields row-by-row instead of batch-by-batch, the\noutput row count does not match the expected input batch size. The Spark Connect\nexecution framework enforces a strict row-count invariant between input and output\nbatches that was not enforced in the classic execution path.\n\n### SC-Compatible Alternative\n\n```python\nfrom pyspark.sql.functions import pandas_udf\nimport pandas as pd\nfrom typing import Iterator\n\n@pandas_udf("long")\ndef my_udf(iterator: Iterator[pd.Series]) -> Iterator[pd.Series]:\n    for batch in iterator:\n        # Yield entire batch at once\n        yield batch * 2\n```\n\n### Notes\n\n- Error: `Output rows does not match input rows` (or similar wording\n  `Output row count does not match input row count`).\n- The fix is to always yield a full `pd.Series` or `pd.DataFrame` per input batch, not\n  individual rows.\n\n---\n\n## Pattern: MLflow non-allowlisted API integrations\n\n**Severity:** P1\n**Affected Compute:** Standard, Serverless\n**Languages:** Python\n**DBR Fix Version:** None (tracked)\n\n### Incompatible Code\n\n```python\nimport mlflow\n\n# Various MLflow integrations that internally use non-allowlisted\n# Spark APIs (e.g., JVM access, SparkContext methods)\nmlflow.spark.autolog()\nmlflow.spark.log_model(spark_model, "model")\n```\n\n### Why It Fails\n\nMLflow\'s Databricks integrations internally call Spark APIs that are not on the Spark\nConnect allowlist. These include JVM interactions for model serialization, SparkContext\naccess for run metadata, and other internal hooks that require JVM-side Spark APIs not available on Spark Connect.\n\n### SC-Compatible Alternative\n\n```python\nimport mlflow\n\n# Use MLflow APIs that do not depend on Spark internals\nwith mlflow.start_run():\n    mlflow.log_param("param1", value)\n    mlflow.log_metric("metric1", value)\n    # Use pandas-based model logging instead of spark model logging\n    mlflow.sklearn.log_model(sklearn_model, "model")\n    mlflow.pyfunc.log_model("model", python_model=my_model)\n```\n\n### Notes\n\n- Not all MLflow APIs are affected. Core logging, tracking, and non-Spark model flavors\n  work correctly.\n'}}]);
